+## Non-Error rejections
 
-This property of `src/orchestration/chatOrchestrator.ts` is recorded so the hook features that follow specify against real behaviour. This issue does not change it; that is a separate, out-of-scope change owned by no issue in this epic.
-
-- The `catch` gates `onError` on `error instanceof Error` ([chatOrchestrator.ts#L150](../../src/orchestration/chatOrchestrator.ts#L150)), so a rejection that is not an `Error` — a thrown string or object — bypasses `onError` entirely while still propagating to the caller.
+- A provider rejection that is not an `Error` instance wraps the value in a new `Error` with the original as `cause` and passes that wrapper to `onError` once; the original rejection value is re-thrown to the caller unchanged, so a hook typed against `Error` keeps compiling and a hook that wants the raw value can reach it through `cause` ([validated by: calls onError with wrapped Error when provider rejects with a string](../../src/orchestration/chatOrchestrator.acceptance.test.ts#L30)).
+- The same guarantee holds for a plain-object rejection ([validated by: calls onError with wrapped Error when provider rejects with a plain object](../../src/orchestration/chatOrchestrator.acceptance.test.ts#L58)).
+- The same guarantee holds when the rejection value is `undefined` ([validated by: calls onError with wrapped Error when provider rejects with undefined](../../src/orchestration/chatOrchestrator.acceptance.test.ts#L86)).
